\begin{description}
\item[* name:] taktactivity2
\item[* relevant examples:] x1 push x2, x1 push, x1 go
\item[* language:] English
\item[* kind of rule:] M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] VERBtoVERBPPROP
\item[* class:] Aktionsartcalculation transformations
\item[* date of creation:] 27-JAN-1988
\item[* author:] Lisette Appelo
\item[* copied from:] Taktactivity2 Spanish LA
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author: 
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] Calculate the value for the attribute {\em aktionsarts}
on basis of 
properties of the main VERB (attribute {\em classes})
 and properties of the arguments
. In this rule a subject, object, indobject  or prepobject argument are
allowed (but not needed) and there are no restrictions 
on properties of these arguments. A directional argument is not allowed except 
for directional arguments that are part of an idiom or EMPTY.
This rule is for verbs with type {\em 
movementclass}.
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
